### This gets all the contacts from the database and returns them as a JSON array. 
GET http://localhost:8080/contacts

### Get contact by id.
GET http://localhost:8080/contacts/69fe552ab52f6f618b40f24a

### Create contact.
POST http://localhost:8080/contacts HTTP/1.1    
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Manuel",
    "lastName": "Jordan",
    "email": "manueljordan@gmail.com",
    "favoriteColor": "pink",
    "birthday": "04/04/1944"
}

### Update contact. 
PUT http://localhost:8080/contacts/6a078b459b060f751275f8f3 HTTP/1.1    
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Manuel",
    "lastName": "Jordan",
    "email": "manueljordan@gmail.com",
    "favoriteColor": "orange",
    "birthday": "04/04/1944"
}

### Delete contact.   
DELETE http://localhost:8080/contacts/6a078b459b060f751275f8f3